WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.520
The Fifty Shades series is back on the big
screen with stars Dakota Johnson and Jamie

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.560
Dornan continuing E.L.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.230
James's story of Ana Steele and Christian
Grey.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.010
So, to mark the return of the multi-million-dollar
film franchise, I've put together some crazy,

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.830
intriguing facts about the Fifty Shades movie
sequels.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:23.060
After the first film, some audiences complained
that there weren't enough, erm, shades of

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.060
Dornan on show.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.940
In fact, even the 90-year-old co-editor of
the Shades of Grey movie, Anne Coates, thought

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.150
the film could have been raunchier.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.540
Dakota Johnson also joked that she was going
to start a campaign to get Jamie Dornan 'fully

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.250
naked' in the sequels.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:41.510
And Dornan himself said he thought Hollywood's
double-standards on male and female nudity

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:42.510
were unfair.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:46.550
But while Dornan has also said he's not bothered
about being nude on camera, he's remained

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:52.100
pretty reticent about what exactly is on show
in Shades Darker and Shades Freed, saying,

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.309
just a couple of weeks after filming, that
he couldn't remember.

00:00:55.309 --> 00:01:00.800
Despite that and the rumours that he was offered
over $1 million to reveal all in the sequels,

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.649
the 'Dornan D', as Dakota jokily called it,
remained firmly tucked away in a flesh-coloured

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:09.259
bag during filming, just like it was in Shades
of Grey.

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:13.090
Now that Jamie Dornan's known all over the
world for bringing Christian Grey to life

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:17.409
on the silver screen, there's not many places
he can go without being recognised by fans

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:18.469
of Fifty Shades.

00:01:18.469 --> 00:01:22.840
In fact, the funniest fan interaction he remembers
took place in an elevator.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.189
And no, it was absolutely nothing like that
scene in Fifty Shades Darker!

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:31.530
What actually happened was that, Dornan was
in an elevator when a very drunk woman suddenly

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:35.599
realised who he was and started telling him
that it was thanks to E.L.

00:01:35.599 --> 00:01:39.619
James's erotic novels that she got pregnant
as after reading them she and her husband

00:01:39.619 --> 00:01:41.590
began having a lot more sex!

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:46.200
Shooting the two sequels, Fifty Shades Darker
and Fifty Shades Freed, involved 160 sets

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.649
and locations, and 103 days of filming in
three countries and eight cities.

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:54.429
In fact, one of those locations proved especially
familiar for Jamie Dornan, who by a quirk

00:01:54.429 --> 00:01:59.869
of fate ended up staying in not only the same
hotel but also the exact same room he'd stayed

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:04.920
in when he acted in his very first movie,
Marie Antoinette, over 10 years previously.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:09.250
And if that wasn't enough of a déjà-vu experience
for Dornan, for the Fifty Shades sequels,

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.890
he also filmed at the opera house by the hotel,
the very place where he shot his first-ever

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.430
scene as an actor.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:19.340
And on top of that, the cinematographer on
Fifty Shades Darker and Fifty Shades Freed

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.890
is John Schwartzman, who's the cousin of Marie
Antoinette writer and director Sofia Coppola

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:28.780
and the brother of Jason Schwartzman, who
starred in Marie Antoinette along with Jamie!

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:32.760
The biggest, most demanding sequence for the
movie's crew was the masquerade ball at the

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.030
Grey family mansion that features in Fifty
Shades Darker.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:40.120
When she was writing the book, EL James based
the scene on her own experience throwing two

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.420
masquerade balls.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:45.600
But the filmmakers went for a different look
to the 'very restrained' 'pastel affair' that

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.350
James says she imagined when writing.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:51.250
However, they did tip their hat to the novel
when it came to things like the menu, wine

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.710
and auction items.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.710
Production designer Nelson Coates was inspired
by the lavish looks of Venice and its mask-filled

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:02.530
Carnival, and even re-created an old Venetian
cathedral floor at the Vancouver Convention

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.510
Centre where they filmed the ball.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:08.750
Amid all the extravagance of the masquerade
scene, costume designer Shay Cunliffe wanted

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:13.190
to keep Ana's look minimal, making her stand
out as, what she calls, a 'beautiful siren

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.320
of simplicity'.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:20.670
So, Ana's gown channels old Hollywood, especially
1930s musicals, and was created by LA-based

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:25.110
fashion designer Monique Lhuillier, whose
clientele include Reese Witherspoon and Scarlett

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:26.110
Johansson.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:30.030
And every single feather in the cape that
Ana wears as she enters the ball was sewn

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.690
on by hand.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:36.120
Dressing the scene's more than 200 extras
proved trickier than the filmmakers first

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.120
thought.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.380
Initially, they turned to the costume houses
Tirelli in Rome and Malabar in Toronto to

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:42.650
hire period outfits.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:48.360
But then the scene began looking like an 18th-century
play, so they sent the outfits back, and instead

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:53.510
went for a mix of costume pieces along with
formal party wear including 1980s couture.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:58.440
In addition to that, they also bought hundreds
of masks from classic mask makers in Venice.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:02.800
The Fifty Shades sequels give even more insight
into Christian's billionaire lifestyle.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.850
For example, several new rooms were added
to his penthouse that weren't seen in the

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:11.960
previous film, including a library and billiard
room, that's home to a very special Brunswick

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:17.039
Centennial Art Deco pool table, which is a
limited edition collectors' item from just

00:04:17.039 --> 00:04:18.989
after the Second World War.

00:04:18.989 --> 00:04:24.410
The room also houses an especially distinctive
$17,000-dollar chess set by designer Kelly

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:30.159
Wearstler that features a hand-sculpted marble
board and gold and gunmetal-plated bronze

00:04:30.159 --> 00:04:35.300
pieces in the shape of human body parts including
hands, legs, lips, and torsos.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:39.330
Forget the clean-shaven Christian from Fifty
Shades of Grey, the new movie in the series

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:42.849
hasn't just gone darker, it's also gone stubblier.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:47.330
After complaints that Jamie Dornan wasn't
sporting his usual bearded look in the first

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:51.529
film, the filmmakers decided that stubble
was the way forward for Christian Grey's face

00:04:51.529 --> 00:04:52.650
in the sequels.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:57.090
Which has not only pleased fans who love their
leading man with added facial fuzz, but also

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:59.639
Dornan himself who absolutely hates shaving!

00:04:59.639 --> 00:05:04.159
In fact, the Northern Irish actor has actually
said that he hates his face when it's beardless

00:05:04.159 --> 00:05:06.349
because it makes him look too young.

00:05:06.349 --> 00:05:10.710
And since Dornan feels more at ease with himself
when he's unshaven, he always tries to stay

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.290
that way in each new role he takes on.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:17.849
The Fifty Shades franchise may have played
a big part in Dakota Johnson and Jamie Dornan's

00:05:17.849 --> 00:05:21.699
lives, catapulting them to worldwide fame,
but their nearest and dearest have yet to

00:05:21.699 --> 00:05:25.060
see them on screen as Ana and Christian, and
probably never will.

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:29.599
Yes, although Dakota's parents, Working Girl
star Melanie Griffith and Miami Vice star

00:05:29.599 --> 00:05:33.349
Don Johnson, are both experienced actors themselves,
the thought of watching their daughter in

00:05:33.349 --> 00:05:36.300
the Fifty Shades films is just too uncomfortable.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:40.460
Indeed, Dakota had a bit of an argument about
the subject with Melanie on the red carpet

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:44.699
at the 2015 Oscars, but didn't succeed in
changing her mind.

00:05:44.699 --> 00:05:48.659
But mum Melanie does know what she's talking
about when she says it would be just 'too

00:05:48.659 --> 00:05:53.499
awkward' to watch the movies, as she actually
read all the Fifty Shades books well before

00:05:53.499 --> 00:05:55.400
her daughter auditioned for the role!

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.490
However, Melanie's decision to skip the movies
means she'll miss out on a little surprise

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.849
tribute to her in Fifty Shades Darker, though
Dakota hopes she'll at least see a clip of

00:06:03.849 --> 00:06:05.190
that one particular moment.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:09.699
As for Jamie Dornan, he's said himself that
Christian Grey's not the sort of guy he'd

00:06:09.699 --> 00:06:14.039
hang out with and that the stuff Grey does
in the Fifty Shades movies doesn't float his

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:19.080
or his wife's boat, and likewise he understands
why his wife, actress-composer Amelia Warner,

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.970
doesn't want to watch the movies.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:25.169
And after all, the birth of the couple's daughters,
the first child three days before filming

00:06:25.169 --> 00:06:29.729
kicked off on Shades of Grey, and the second,
two weeks before the sequels started shooting,

00:06:29.729 --> 00:06:33.680
is more than enough for Amelia to remember
her husband's stint as Christian Grey!

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:37.050
So guys, what do you think about the Fifty
Shades movies?

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:39.250
And how do you think they compare to the books?

